diff --git a/ANSWER.md b/ANSWER.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..87ce875
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ANSWER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Why the nightly review never reported anything
+
+The job *does* run: `launchctl print` shows `runs = 6` (one per night since
+it was loaded on 2026-10-12) and `last exit code = 1`. Each run left the same
+two lines in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`:
+
+    Not logged in · Please run /login
+    /Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status
+
+Two separate bugs combine to give "nothing at all":
+
+## 1. The failure path crashes before it can notify (why you got no failure note)
+
+`nightly-review.zsh` runs under zsh and does `status=$?`. In zsh, `status` is
+a read-only special parameter (an alias for `$?`). Assigning to it is a fatal
+error in a non-interactive script: zsh prints `read-only variable: status`
+and exits with code 1 right there, on line 19. The `if` that calls
+`notify.sh` with "nightly review FAILED" is never reached. (This would also
+have hidden any *success*: every run dies on that line regardless of how
+`claude` exited.)
+
+Reproduce: `zsh -c 'false; status=$?; echo after'` → error, no `after`.
+
+**Fix:** rename the variable to `rc`.
+
+## 2. `claude` is not authenticated in the launchd environment (why there was a failure)
+
+`claude -p` exits with `Not logged in · Please run /login`. launchd does not
+start your login shell, so nothing from `~/.zshrc` / `~/.zprofile` is in the
+job's environment (the plist only sets `PATH`) — e.g. an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`
+or token you export there isn't visible, and the interactive login's
+credentials aren't reachable by the headless 02:30 process.
+
+**Fix (needs you, once):** create a long-lived token for unattended use and
+give it to the job via a private env file that the script now sources:
+
+    claude setup-token                      # prints a token
+    mkdir -p ~/.config/nightly-review
+    printf 'export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=%s\n' '<token>' > ~/.config/nightly-review/env
+    chmod 600 ~/.config/nightly-review/env
+
+(Or put `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...` there if you use an API key.) It's a good idea
+to also add `export TG_BOT_TOKEN=...` there, so `notify.sh` doesn't depend on
+the keychain being reachable from launchd at 02:30.
+
+Then test without waiting for the night:
+
+    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review
+    tail ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err
+
+## Changes made to `bin/nightly-review.zsh`
+
+- `status` → `rc` (cause 1).
+- Sources `~/.config/nightly-review/env` if present (cause 2).
+- Passes `--allowedTools` for read-only tools (`Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`,
+  `git log/show/diff`): in `-p` mode Claude can't ask for permission, so
+  without this it couldn't run `git log` once logged in.
+- Captures `claude`'s stderr to `$OUT.err` and includes it in the failure
+  message, so a failure note says *why* (e.g. "Not logged in").
+- Sends the last 3 lines (the phone summary the prompt asks for at the end)
+  instead of the first 300 bytes.
+
+No changes needed to the plist or `notify.sh`; nothing was loaded, run, or
+sent anywhere.
diff --git a/bin/nightly-review.zsh b/bin/nightly-review.zsh
index e0b986f..eb80c08 100755
--- a/bin/nightly-review.zsh
+++ b/bin/nightly-review.zsh
@@ -6,6 +6,14 @@ REPO="$HOME/projects/shop"
 OUT="$HOME/Library/Logs/nightly-review-$(date +%F).md"
 NOTIFY="$HOME/bin/notify.sh"
 
+# launchd does not run your login shell, so nothing from ~/.zshrc/.zprofile
+# (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, ...) is visible here.
+# Put the credentials the job needs in this file (chmod 600), e.g.
+#   export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...   # from `claude setup-token`
+#   export TG_BOT_TOKEN=...
+ENV_FILE="$HOME/.config/nightly-review/env"
+[ -r "$ENV_FILE" ] && source "$ENV_FILE"
+
 SINCE=$(date -v-1d +%F)
 PROMPT="Review the commits in this repository since $SINCE.
 For each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky
@@ -15,12 +23,18 @@ Do not modify any file."
 
 cd "$REPO" || { "$NOTIFY" "nightly review: repo missing"; exit 1; }
 
-claude -p "$PROMPT" --output-format text > "$OUT"
-status=$?
+# Headless mode can't prompt for permissions, so pre-approve read-only tools.
+# Capture stderr too, so a failure note can say what went wrong.
+claude -p "$PROMPT" --output-format text \
+  --allowedTools "Read" "Grep" "Glob" "Bash(git log:*)" "Bash(git show:*)" "Bash(git diff:*)" \
+  > "$OUT" 2> "$OUT.err"
+# NB: `status` is a read-only special parameter in zsh (alias of $?); use rc.
+rc=$?
 
-if [ $status -ne 0 ]; then
-  "$NOTIFY" "nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT"
-  exit $status
+if [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then
+  "$NOTIFY" "nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(head -c 300 "$OUT.err") — see $OUT.err"
+  exit $rc
 fi
 
-"$NOTIFY" "nightly review done: $(head -c 300 "$OUT")"
+# The phone summary is at the end of the output, so send the tail.
+"$NOTIFY" "nightly review done: $(tail -n 3 "$OUT")"
